      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T15:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a bit of an odd design to publicly inherit SkNWayCanvas but then go and hide the public APIs of SkNWayCanvas.\n\nI\u0027m still in favor of the other approach we talked about last week where `SkCaptureCanvas` just holds two `std::unique_ptr\u003cSkCanvas\u003e` where the recording canvas is null if not active.  Then we can extend SkCanvasVirtualEnforcer\u003cSkCaptureCanvas\u003e\n\nA macro can be used to make most overrides pretty lightweight:\n\n```\n#define CALL_CANVAS(FN, ...) \\\n    this-\u003epollCapturingStatus(); \\\n    fBaseCanvas-\u003eFN(__VA_ARGS__); \\\n    if (fRecordingCanvas) { \\\n        fRecordingCanvas-\u003eFN(__VA_ARGS__); \\\n    }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "cfcee4db26a92681f57d3103c72d7c54ccf5e4bd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
